assessment.verification_assessment:
Acceptance is observable through an isolated rehearsal with pinned fixture evidence. Each of these can be checked by an independent verifier on the exact published SHA:
- quiescence achieved;
- active work and effects reconciled durably;
- checkpoint integrity verified;
- pending reservations retained;
- rollback produces no duplication;
- a concurrent Node/Python writer is rejected;
- negative controls discriminate.

These are coupled properties of one substrate, so a single independent verdict is meaningful. Two limits apply. The verdict is only as strong as the FX-E2 fixture, which is still unpinned, so fixture pinning is the first gate. The verdict covers local or isolated proof only. Per the task's own evidence rules, it cannot establish operational or live success.
